oRmdQellDNE9PY01IcDhTQWFBZzJUbUxTeEowUVRNS1R1QnpCWHJhU0h1bDJS?oc=5","date":"2026-09-24","zh":"Invitation Homes 第二季度表現強勁，成長強勁..."}],"themes":[{"name":"分析師評等","count":3},{"name":"財報","count":2},{"name":"股票回購/股利","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-19","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1687229/000168722926000016/invh-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Invitation Homes is a leading owner and operator of single-family homes for lease, offering residents high-quality homes in sought-after neighborhoods across the United States. As of December 31, 2025, we wholly own 86,192 homes for lease, jointly own 8,006 homes for lease, and provide professional third-party property and asset management services for an additional 15,866 homes, all of which are primarily located in 16 core markets across the country. These homes help meet the needs of a growing share of Americans who count on the ease, flexibility, and savings of leasing. We provide our residents access to updated homes with features they value, as well as close proximity to jobs and good schools. The continued demand for our product proves that the choice and flexibility we offer are attractive to many people.","zh":"Invitation Homes 是一家領先的單戶住宅租賃業主和營運商，在美國各地的熱門社區為居民提供高品質住宅。截至2025年12月31日，我們全資擁有86,192套出租房屋，共同擁有8,006套出租房屋，並為另外15,866套房屋提供專業的第三方物業和資產管理服務，所有這些房屋主要分佈在全國16個核心市場。這些房屋有助於滿足越來越多依賴租賃的便利性、靈活性和節省成本的美國人的需求。我們為居民提供更新的住宅，提供他們重視的功能，並且靠近工作場所和好學校。對我們產品的持續需求證明我們提供的選擇和靈活性對許多人有吸引力。"},{"en":"We operate in markets with strong demand drivers, high barriers to entry, and high rent growth potential, primarily in the Western United States, Florida, and the Southeast United States. Through disciplined market and asset selection, as well as through strategic mergers and acquisitions, we designed our wholly and jointly owned portfolios to capture the operating benefits of local density as well as economies of scale that we believe cannot be readily replicated. Since our founding in 2012, we have built a proven, vertically integrated operating platform that enables us to effectively and efficiently acquire, renovate, lease, maintain, and manage both the homes we own and those we manage on behalf of others.","zh":"我們在需求驅動強勁、進入障礙高、租金成長潛力大的市場開展業務，主要是在美國西部、佛羅裡達州和美國東南部。透過嚴格的市場和資產選擇，以及策略併購，我們設計了全資和合資投資組合，以獲取當地密度的營運效益以及我們認為無法輕易複製的規模經濟。自 2012 年成立以來，我們建立了一個經過驗證的垂直整合營運平台，使我們能夠有效且有效率地收購、翻新、租賃、維護和管理我們擁有的房屋以及我們代表他人管理的房屋。"},{"en":"The portfolio of homes we own average approximately 1,880 square feet with three to four bedrooms and two bathrooms, appealing to a resident base that we believe is less transitory than a typical multifamily resident. We invest in the upfront renovation of homes in our portfolio in order to address capital needs, reduce ongoing maintenance costs, and drive resident demand.","zh":"我們擁有的住宅組合平均面積約為 1,880 平方英尺，設有三到四間臥室和兩間浴室，對我們認為比典型多戶居民來說更短暫的居民基礎很有吸引力。我們對投資組合中的房屋進行前期翻新投資，以滿足資本需求、降低持續維護成本並推動居民需求。"}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"We face competition from different sources in each of our primary activities: acquiring and leasing our properties and providing property and asset management services for single-family homes. We believe our competitors in acquiring or building homes for investment purposes are larger investors, including private equity funds and other REITs, that are seeking to capitalize on the same market opportunity that we have identified, and individual investors or small private investment partnerships, that are seeking investment properties that can either be leased or restored and sold. Our primary competitors in acquiring portfolios include large and small private equity investors, public and private REITs, and other sizable private institutional investors. These same competitors may also compete with us for residents and may provide property and asset management services similar to those that ","zh":"我們在每項主要活動中都面臨著來自不同來源的競爭：收購和租賃我們的房產以及為單戶住宅提供房產和資產管理服務。我們認為，我們在出於投資目的收購或建造房屋方面的競爭對手是較大的投資者，包括私募股權基金和其他房地產投資信託基金，他們正在尋求利用我們所發現的同一市場機會，以及個人投資者或小型私人投資合夥企業，他們正在尋求可以租賃或恢復和出售的投資房產。我們在收購投資組合方面的主要競爭對手包括大型和小型私募股權投資者、公共和私人房地產投資信託基金以及其他大型私人機構投資者。這些相同的競爭對手也可能與我們競爭居民，並可能提供類似那些的物業和資產管理服務"},{"en":"In addition, federal, state, and local regulatory developments, including executive actions and proposed federal and state legislation aimed at limiting institutional ownership and acquisition of single-family homes, may affect the competitive dynamics in our markets by imposing requirements or restrictions that apply differently to various categories of market participants. To the extent these developments disproportionately affect institutional owners, including us, or advantage other categories of investors, such as individual investors and smaller partnerships who may fall outside regulatory definitions, our ability to compete for acquisitions, residents, or capital on favorable terms could be adversely affected. See Part I. Item 1A. \"Risk Factors — Risks Related to Our Business and Operations — Executive actions and proposed federal and state legislation or regulations aimed at limi","zh":"此外，聯邦、州和地方監管的發展，包括旨在限制機構所有權和購買單戶住宅的行政行動和擬議的聯邦和州立法，可能會透過對不同類別的市場參與者施加不同的要求或限制，從而影響我們市場的競爭動態。如果這些發展對包括我們在內的機構所有者產生不成比例的影響，或者使其他類別的投資者受益，例如可能超出監管定義的個人投資者和小型合夥企業，那麼我們以優惠條件競爭收購、居民或資本的能力可能會受到不利影響。請參閱第一部分第 1A 項。 「風險因素 - 與我們的業務和營運相關的風險 - 旨在限制的行政行動和擬議的聯邦和州立法或法規"}],"segments":{},"peers":["AMH","MAA","CPT","UDR","SUI"]}}